    "acl": null,
    "content": "---\nlab_source_id: source-7ee04b58a1c1d981\ntitle: Structural basis of nucleosome binding by the tardigrade damage suppressor protein\nstable_identifier: 10.5555/synthetic.dsup.2018.009\ncanonical_url: \npublished_at: 2018-02-11\nsource_type: journal_article\nvenue: Structural Biology Letters\nlicense: unknown\nauthors: Wei Chen, Nadia Haddad\nprovider: fixtures\n---\n\n# Structural basis of nucleosome binding by the tardigrade damage suppressor protein\n\nA cryo-EM structure of Dsup bound to the nucleosome core particle at 3.4 angstrom resolution shows that the protein engages the acidic patch through a bipartite basic motif and drapes across the DNA gyres. Binding does not distort the histone octamer. The structure explains sequence-independent association and predicts that protection operates by steric occlusion of the DNA surface from diffusing hydroxyl radicals rather than by radical scavenging.",
